 \end{abstract}
 
 \noindent\textbf{Keywords:} autonomous ML research; neural architecture search; Transformer efficiency; multi-objective optimization; reproducibility
 
 \section{Autonomous research result}\label{partone}
 
-\subsection{The question}\label{sec:question}
-\looseness=-1 In Karpathy's autoresearch \citep{autoresearch}, an AI agent repeatedly edits a language model's training program, trains each version for the same 300\,s on one GPU and keeps an edit only if the model improves. Because the budget is time, a faster program also trains on more data. AutoPareto keeps this loop but gives the agent three objectives: quality, decoding speed and inference memory. \textbf{We ask what the agents discover, how they discover it, and whether the gains survive once speed and training data are separated.}
+\subsection{The question and the setup}\label{sec:question}\label{sec:brief}
