-\textbf{Did Opus game the decode metric?} It stayed within the permitted surface: the adapter had to compute the same outputs, and every variant passed the correctness checks with identical greedy tokens on the 64- and 256-token prefixes they cover. Those checks reach neither the timed window nor the 1{,}024-token ring cache. The 13-recipe test closed this gap for the submitted recipes: every timed token of all 8 prompts, including the ring cache's wrap, matched the uncached model's argmax in all \CRSixCorrectRuns{} runs (\CRSixNearTies{} disagreements within the registered 0.25-logit bfloat16 tie, none outside it). Its records describe graph replay as a fix for launch-bound decode and note the prefill cost (Table~\ref{tab:reasoning}), so it was the metric's definition, not a rule violation, that rewarded the placement. We report decode-only and end-to-end speed side by side and recommend prefill-inclusive scoring.
